{"hash":"xs5aivcjn7","parent_hash":"yluunycalu","title":"Figure 2 plot","created":"2026-06-04T21:44:18.635Z","versionCreatedAt":"2026-06-04T21:44:08.491Z","stateUrl":"https://www.desmos.com/calc-states/production/version/xs5aivcjn7/8415a780-605e-11f1-9a1a-952b65aeb828","thumbUrl":"https://www.desmos.com/calc_thumbs/production/version/xs5aivcjn7/8415a780-605e-11f1-9a1a-952b65aeb828.png","currentVersion":"8415a780-605e-11f1-9a1a-952b65aeb828","type":"my-graph","access":"link","product":"graphing","state":{"version":11,"randomSeed":"c68d5ad309fea1084e13565a01e14f09","graph":{"viewport":{"xmin":-2.906873380843393,"ymin":-3.1313069293971356,"xmax":4.570604214459982,"ymax":4.346170665906006},"xAxisLabel":"s","yAxisLabel":"l","squareAxes":false,"__v12ViewportLatexStash":{"xmin":"-2.906873380843393","xmax":"4.570604214459982","ymin":"-3.1313069293971356","ymax":"4.346170665906006"}},"expressions":{"list":[{"type":"text","id":"97","text":"First we define the parameters for the network in Figure 2. The mixing parameter is γ. The reticulation edges have branch length ε. The horizontal axis is s, the branch lengths of the pendant edge. The vertical axis is \\ell, the branch length of the edge opposite to the reticulation vertex. The parameters v1,...,v5 are rate parameters (all =1 in the paper)."},{"type":"expression","id":"82","color":"#6042a6","latex":"s=x","hidden":true},{"type":"expression","id":"81","color":"#388c46","latex":"l=y","hidden":true},{"type":"expression","id":"55","color":"#2d70b3","latex":"\\varepsilon=0","slider":{"hardMin":true,"hardMax":true,"min":"0","max":"1","step":".01"}},{"type":"expression","id":"74","color":"#c74440","latex":"\\gamma=0.5","slider":{"hardMin":true,"hardMax":true,"min":"0","max":"1","step":".05"}},{"type":"expression","id":"73","color":"#000000","latex":"a_{1}=\\ e^{-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot v_{1}s}","hidden":true},{"type":"expression","id":"135","color":"#388c46","latex":"v_{1}=1","hidden":true,"slider":{"hardMin":true,"hardMax":true,"min":"0","max":"2","step":".05"}},{"type":"expression","id":"72","color":"#6042a6","latex":"a_{2}=\\ e^{-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot v_{2}s}","hidden":true},{"type":"expression","id":"136","color":"#6042a6","latex":"v_{2}=1","hidden":true,"slider":{"hardMin":true,"hardMax":true,"min":"0","max":"2","step":".25"}},{"type":"expression","id":"66","color":"#388c46","latex":"a_{3}=\\ e^{-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot v_{3}s}","hidden":true},{"type":"expression","id":"137","color":"#000000","latex":"v_{3}=1","hidden":true,"slider":{"hardMin":true,"hardMax":true,"min":"0","max":"2","step":".25"}},{"type":"expression","id":"62","color":"#6042a6","latex":"a_{4}=e^{-\\frac{4}{3}v_{4}\\cdot\\varepsilon}","hidden":true},{"type":"expression","id":"140","color":"#388c46","latex":"v_{4}=1","slider":{"hardMin":true,"hardMax":true,"min":"0","max":"2","step":".25"}},{"type":"expression","id":"65","color":"#2d70b3","latex":"a_{5}=e^{-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot v_{5}\\cdot l}","hidden":true},{"type":"expression","id":"145","color":"#388c46","latex":"v_{5}=1","hidden":true,"slider":{"hardMin":true,"hardMax":true,"min":"0","max":"2","step":".25"}},{"type":"expression","id":"64","color":"#c74440","latex":"a_{6}=e^{-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot v_{6}\\cdot\\varepsilon}","hidden":true},{"type":"expression","id":"144","color":"#2d70b3","latex":"v_{6}=1","slider":{"hardMin":true,"hardMax":true,"min":"0","max":"2","step":".25"}},{"type":"text","id":"86","text":"Next define the parameterization for M1, using (q1, q2, q3, q4) = (qACC, qCAC, qCCA, qCGT):"},{"type":"expression","id":"71","color":"#388c46","latex":"q_{1}=a_{2}\\cdot a_{3}\\cdot a_{5}"},{"type":"expression","id":"76","color":"#388c46","latex":"q_{2}=\\gamma\\cdot a_{1}\\cdot a_{3}\\cdot a_{4}\\cdot a_{5}+\\left(1-\\gamma\\right)\\cdot a_{1}\\cdot a_{3}\\cdot a_{6}"},{"type":"expression","id":"77","color":"#6042a6","latex":"q_{3}=\\gamma\\cdot a_{1}\\cdot a_{2}\\cdot a_{4}+\\left(1-\\gamma\\right)\\cdot a_{1}\\cdot a_{2}\\cdot a_{5}\\cdot a_{6}"},{"type":"expression","id":"79","color":"#c74440","latex":"q_{4}=\\gamma\\cdot a_{1}\\cdot a_{2}\\cdot a_{3}\\cdot a_{4}\\cdot a_{5}+\\left(1-\\gamma\\right)\\cdot a_{1}\\cdot a_{2}\\cdot a_{3}\\cdot a_{5}\\cdot a_{6}"},{"type":"text","id":"94","text":"The defining inequalities for M1:"},{"type":"expression","id":"87","color":"#388c46","latex":"q_{1}-q_{4}>0","hidden":true},{"type":"expression","id":"91","color":"#c74440","latex":"q_{4}-q_{1}\\cdot q_{2}>0","hidden":true},{"type":"expression","id":"90","color":"#000000","latex":"q_{1}\\cdot q_{2}\\cdot q_{3}-q_{4}^{2}>0","hidden":true},{"type":"expression","id":"80","color":"#2d70b3","latex":"q_{4}+q_{1}\\cdot\\left(q_{4}-q_{2}-q_{3}\\right)>0","hidden":true},{"type":"text","id":"95","text":"In order for the point (q1,q2,q3,q4) to be in M2, it is necessary and sufficient that it satisfy the following inequality:"},{"type":"expression","id":"78","color":"#c74440","latex":"q_{4}+q_{2}\\cdot\\left(q_{4}-q_{1}-q_{3}\\right)>0\\left\\{x>0\\right\\}\\left\\{y>0\\right\\}","hidden":true},{"type":"text","id":"99","text":"Therefore the following region is the set of points which are distinguishable from M2:"},{"type":"expression","id":"100","color":"#388c46","latex":"q_{4}+q_{2}\\cdot\\left(q_{4}-q_{1}-q_{3}\\right)<0\\left\\{x>0\\right\\}\\left\\{y>0\\right\\}"},{"type":"text","id":"108","text":"Similarly, using the analogous inequality for M3, the following region is the set of points which are distinguishable from M3:"},{"type":"expression","id":"109","color":"#6042a6","latex":"q_{4}+q_{3}\\left(q_{4}-q_{1}-q_{2}\\right)<0\\left\\{x>0\\right\\}\\left\\{y>0\\right\\}","hidden":true},{"type":"text","id":"132","text":"Together, the union of the red region (line 29) and the following orange regions constitute an impossibility zone where no amount of sequence data will be sufficient to infer which species is the hybrid with high probability."},{"type":"expression","id":"128","color":"#fa7e19","latex":"q_{4}+q_{3}\\left(q_{4}-q_{1}-q_{2}\\right)>0\\left\\{x>0\\right\\}\\left\\{y>0\\right\\}","hidden":true},{"type":"text","id":"149","text":"The next inequality is the one of two used in the parameter corollary. It is equivalent to the inequality in line 29."},{"type":"expression","id":"148","color":"#2d70b3","latex":"a_{1}<\\frac{a_{5}}{\\gamma a_{4}a_{5}+(1-\\gamma)a_{4}}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\gamma a_{4}(1-a_{3}a_{5})+(1-\\gamma)a_{4}(1-a_{3})}{\\gamma a_{4}(1-a_{3}a_{5})+a_{5}(1-\\gamma)a_{4}(1-a_{3})}\\right)\\left\\{x>0\\right\\}\\left\\{y>0\\right\\}","hidden":true}]},"includeFunctionParametersInRandomSeed":true,"doNotMigrateMovablePointStyle":true}}